  "summary": "whalibmob 5.33.18: unverified network/filesystem patterns in library modules",
  "details": "The package ships library modules that co-locate filesystem reads with HTTP/HTTPS request primitives (lib/MediaService.js imports fs/http/https and performs fs.readFileSync alongside https.request), and references ping/curl/ps alongside network calls in lib/Registration.js, lib/WebVersion.js, and lib/socks.js. The flagged content appears in library files rather than lifecycle hooks, and the keyword co-occurrence alone does not identify a specific installer-side data read, a specific attacker-controlled destination, or an install/import-time auto-execution path. The name is a close variant of a well-known library name, which raises typosquat suspicion but is not by itself proof of malicious code.",
